OL,3,GNEWSAClosing date looms for decades-old
OL,4,Acity joke store
OL,5,
OL,6,FA joke and costume shop that has been
OL,7,Fin a city centre since 1992 will close
OL,8,Ffor good at the end of the year unless
OL,9,Fa new buyer is found.
OL,11,FSara Hennessy, who owns Jokers Corner
OL,12,Fin Far Gosford Street, Coventry, put
OL,13,Fthe store up for sale last year in the
OL,14,Fhope it would remain a joke shop after
OL,15,Fit changed hands, but said she had not
OL,16,Fyet found anyone to take it on.
OL,18,FThe business owner said she made the
OL,19,Fsad decision to close up so she could
OL,20,Fhave more time to look after her four
OL,21,Fchildren, and added it was struggling
OL,22,Ffinancially.
OL,23,APub: 22-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,354,350,200,160,0,100
